Changes by PQC Today, LLC (2026)
--------------------------------
Modified from strongSwan 6.0.5 (each file carries a "Modified by" line):
  Makefile.am           adds pkcs11_kem.c/.h to the plugin sources
  pkcs11.h              PKCS#11 v3.2 key types, mechanisms, attributes and
                        parameter sets for ML-KEM, ML-DSA and SLH-DSA
  pkcs11_dh.c           keeps the ECDH peer value alive until derive; marks the
                        derived secret readable (CKA_SENSITIVE/CKA_EXTRACTABLE)
  pkcs11_plugin.c       registers the ML-KEM key exchange and PQC signature
                        types; stops advertising MODP groups the token lacks
  pkcs11_private_key.c  ML-DSA, SLH-DSA, Ed448 and Ed25519 signing via the token
  pkcs11_public_key.c   ML-DSA, SLH-DSA, Ed448 and Ed25519 public keys and
                        verification, SubjectPublicKeyInfo handling
New files written by PQC Today, LLC, under the same GPL-2.0-or-later terms:
  pkcs11_kem.c, pkcs11_kem.h, test_ss.c, tests/, README.md
All other files are unchanged from strongSwan 6.0.5 (the same files differ
from strongSwan 6.0.7, the baseline of ../strongswan-pkcs11.patch).

The complete change set against a pristine strongSwan tree is
../strongswan-pkcs11.patch (regenerate it with
../regen-strongswan-pkcs11-patch.sh). The WebAssembly build applies further
patches to strongSwan itself: ../strongswan-6.0.5-pqc.patch,
../strongswan-6.0.5-wasm.patch and the shims in ../strongswan-wasm-shims/,
driven by ../scripts/build-strongswan-wasm.sh.

